{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat readback/watch-notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# What the watch showed for event 184233 (Tempo run 45)\n\nIntervals: LTHR 172. Watch (Forerunner 965): auto-detected LTHR 168, zones\nZ1 <118, Z2 118–137, Z3 137–151, Z4 151–162, Z5 >162.\n\n`GET /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events/184233` returned the event exactly as we sent\nit (see `event-184233-as-sent.json`); `workout_doc.steps` is populated, so the\nAPI accepted it.\n\n| step | planned (% LTHR) | expected on watch (× 172) | watch displayed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Warm-up easy | 68–75 | 117–129 | 118–137 |\n| Tempo | 88–93 | 151–160 | 151–162 |\n| Float | 75–82 | 129–141 | 137–151 |\n| Cool-down | 65–72 | 112–124 | 118–137 |\n\nEvery corridor shows up as one of the watch's own zone bands, not the range we\nplanned. Changing the watch's LTHR to 172 moves the bands but they are still\nzone edges, never 151–160 or 129–141. Earlier tries: `units: \"bpm\"` with\nabsolute values made the watch show 214–249 bpm; `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` made\nevery target a constant 101.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat README.md'","aggregated_output":"# tri-planner\n\nGenerates structured triathlon workouts and pushes them to Intervals.icu, which\nexports them to the athlete's Garmin watch through Garmin Connect.\n\n- `gen.py` turns a plan (`plans/*.json`) into the body for\n  `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` (an event with `workout_doc`).\n- `push.sh` posts it (needs `INTERVALS_API_KEY` and `ATHLETE_ID`).\n- `readback/` holds what the API returned for the last pushed event and\n  notes on what the watch displayed.\n\nAthlete thresholds live in Intervals (LTHR 172 for this athlete). HR targets\nin plans are percentages of LTHR; Intervals converts them to bpm at export.\n\n```\npython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json\n./push.sh event.json\n```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat gen.py'","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Build an Intervals.icu event body (workout_doc) from a plan file.\n\nUsage: python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport sys\n\n\ndef hr_target(step):\n    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n\n\ndef build_step(step):\n    out = {\"duration\": step[\"minutes\"] * 60}\n    if \"hr_pct\" in step:\n        out[\"hr\"] = hr_target(step)\n    if \"label\" in step:\n        out[\"text\"] = step[\"label\"]\n    return out\n\n\ndef build_doc(plan):\n    steps = []\n    for block in plan[\"steps\"]:\n        if \"repeat\" in block:\n            steps.append({\n                \"reps\": block[\"repeat\"],\n                \"steps\": [build_step(s) for s in block[\"steps\"]],\n            })\n        else:\n            steps.append(build_step(block))\n    return {\"steps\": steps}\n\n\ndef build_event(plan):\n    return {\n        \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\n        \"type\": plan[\"sport\"],\n        \"name\": plan[\"name\"],\n        \"start_date_local\": plan[\"date\"] + \"T00:00:00\",\n        \"workout_doc\": build_doc(plan),\n    }\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    with open(sys.argv[1]) as f:\n        plan = json.load(f)\n    json.dump(build_event(plan), sys.stdout, indent=2)\n    print()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
